What is AuthenticationEntryPoint?

It is the component that Spring Security calls when an unauthenticated user tries to access a protected resource.

Example:

GET /api/v1/orders

Authorization: (missing)

Flow:

Client
   │
   ▼
Security Filter Chain
   │
   ▼
JwtAuthenticationFilter
   │
   ▼
No Authentication Found
   │
   ▼
AuthenticationEntryPoint
   │
   ▼
401 Unauthorized JSON

Without it, Spring Security returns its default error response.

With it, every 401 response matches your ApiResponse format.

Difference Between 401 and 403

This is one of the most common interview questions.

Scenario	Status Code	Handler
No JWT	401 Unauthorized	AuthenticationEntryPoint
Invalid JWT	401 Unauthorized	AuthenticationEntryPoint
Expired JWT	401 Unauthorized	AuthenticationEntryPoint
Valid JWT but insufficient role	403 Forbidden	AccessDeniedHandler

Example:

No Token
